node.doctext:
I like to use the following subroutine by passing it a directory name as such:
<p>

<code>my @sourcefiles = &get_files($source_directory);</code>

</p>The subroutine along the lines of:

<code>sub get_files {
	my $files = shift;
	my @file_list;
	opendir(DIR, $files) or die "Can't open directory, $!\n";
	@file_list = readdir(DIR);
	closedir(DIR);
	# Removing directory references '.' and '..' from the listing
	my $rmdir = shift (@file_list);
	my $rmdir2 = shift (@file_list);
	return @file_list;
}
</code>

I have some other versions too but can't find them at the minute... but this will get you the full file path and thus file and you can play around with the array/list that is returned. </p></p>
